      "extract": "We begin by deﬁning the notion of negative dependence commonly found in the literature. Negative Cylinder Dependence. A collection of Boolean random variables X1, . . . , Xn is said to be negative cylinder dependent if for every S ⊆[n], E \u0002\u0003 i∈S Xi \u0004 ≤\u0003 i∈S E [Xi] and E \u0002\u0003 i∈S (1 −Xi) \u0004 ≤\u0003 i∈S E [1 −Xi] . Negative cylinder dependence is the weaker notion considered here. It is known to imply Chernoff bounds for",
      "extractCut": true
    },
