      "extract": "We will now prove our main result. As mentioned in the introduction, our proof is based on the standard technique of bounding the exponential moments, which can be enhanced using the p-th moment method. The following lemma contains our main technical contribution, which implies that the exponential moments of f (X1, . . . , Xn) under 1-negative association are dominated by that under independence. Our results will",
