      "extract": "In this subsection, we illustrate an application of our proof technique to give concen- tration for a read-k family of supermodular functions. Read-k families arise naturally in problems such as subgraph counting in random graphs, and can be seen as a comple- mentary weak dependence notion to that of low-degree polynomials [29]. Our work gives the ﬁrst concentration results for these problems under negative",
